  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Procurement Reform and Capacity Building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Component 1: Strengthening Institutional Capacity and Legal Framework:  The focus of this component is to strengthen the new institutional arrangement imposed by the new procurement law and address the inconsistency of the legal framework with international best practice. It is also expected that the grant will increase the overall capacity for public service delivery and the efficiency of the HATC and the HTB, to ensure Government effective implementation and enforcement of the new procurement law. Activity1: Improving the existing institutional arrangement and legal frame work The assessment will include reviewing the procurement law no23, 2007, its executive regulations, the institutional arrangements, and the efficiency of the system. The report will present the findings and provide recommendations for further improvement.</narrative>
  </description>
